      "content": "okay, i'll try thinning out the bevel to 20 degrees and see if that helps with the tearing. i'll also check the moisture levels with my meter. thanks for the tip. \n\none more thing—you mentioned the edge might be \"too sharp\" causing splits. i've always thought sharper is always better in joinery, so that's a weird thought. can you explain how a super sharp edge would actually cause more damage to the wood than a slightly duller one?",
